      "body": "Concept ACK\n\nThere are lots of AI findings about these potential misconfigurations, so it would be good to close off as many of them as possible in one go.\n\nA few closely related cases seem worth covering as well:\n- `-timeout` values above `INT_MAX` are narrowed before the new positivity check (similar ones were already attempted here and closed).\n- Very large `-mempoolexpiry` values can overflow when converted from hours to seconds.\n- A negative `-txconfirmtarget` wraps into the wallet's unsigned target and can make fee estimation fall back to `-fallbackfee`.\n- Negating an integer option is documented as setting it to `0`, so `-nolimitclustersize` and `-nobantime` are equivalent to the zero values this PR explicitly accepts. `-limitclustersize=0` makes every transaction oversized and prevents normal mempool admission, while `-bantime=0` makes `setban` without an explicit duration create an immediately expired ban.\n\nCI seems to fail because the new test loop binds a `std::string` reference to temporary strings.",
