      "updated_at": "2026-11-13T22:56:43Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Concept ACK 1ab3f148582c21054dfc9323623edcf9768949f6 for parsing improvements here, but I'd recommend against increased use of the DISALLOW_NEGATION flag:\n\n- If your option can't accept zero values, DISALLOW_NEGATION is only a partial fix and may allow zeroes to slip through because you are only guarding against them being set ib a single path. Better to check for valid values one place instead of multiple.\n- It creates inconsistent UX where -option=0 and -nooption have different behaviors without a clear reason, when normal behavior is for them to behave the same.\n\nDISALLOW_NEGATION was intended to used rarely and eventually removed (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/22766#issuecomment-944924866) and this PR seems to increase usage by a lot. The other changes here look very good though.\n\n",
